Subject: [PATCH] staging: t2bce_audio: pair hibernation image callbacks

The audio function owns coherent DMA buffers and BCE command queues, but its PM
table only exposes suspend and resume.  Hibernation therefore invokes the BCE
client prepare hook to revoke bridgeOS remote access without disabling the
audio PCI function, and it never invokes the matching audio resume callback on
thaw or image restore.

Use the existing stateful suspend and resume paths for the in-place freeze,
thaw, and restore lifecycle.  The BCE device link orders the audio consumer
around its core supplier, while the existing deferred-resume callback waits for
VHCI reconstruction before granting bridgeOS remote access again.  Leave
poweroff unset because cold S4 still needs a separate no-state policy.

--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_audio/audio.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_audio/audio.c
@@ -919,6 +919,9 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(pci, t2audio_ids);
 struct dev_pm_ops t2audio_pci_driver_pm = {
         .suspend = t2audio_suspend,
-        .resume = t2audio_resume
+        .resume = t2audio_resume,
+        .freeze = t2audio_suspend,
+        .thaw = t2audio_resume,
+        .restore = t2audio_resume
 };
 struct pci_driver t2audio_pci_driver = {
         .name = "t2bce_audio",
